155-// SetCookiesBestEffort injects cookies one Storage.setCookies call at a
156-// time using the {cookies:[...]} envelope, degrading rather than
157-// aborting. A cookie Chrome rejects (e.g. a __Host- cookie captured
158-// with a Domain, which Storage.setCookies refuses) is logged by name
159-// and value length and skipped; the remaining cookies are still set.
160-// The account-page browser must stay open until the user closes it, so
161-// a non-fatal cookie failure must not bubble up as a flow error.
162-//
163-// CookieInjectionResult reports how many cookies were injected and
164-// which names failed, by name only — no value is ever logged. The
165-// caller decides whether an all-failed result is fatal.
166-type CookieInjectionResult struct {
167-	Injected int
168-	Failed   []string
169-}
170-
